The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` (the second element) instead of `parts[0]` (the first element). This caused it to return the wrong word for multi-word strings and crash for single-word strings.

The fix changed line 4 from `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`, which correctly returns the first word from the space-separated string.
